course: dictionary
lesson: 5735
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lot is a small word with several meanings, so check the words around it. Context clues show you which meaning fits. «Animation is lots of still pictures, shown so fast that they blend into movement.» Here lots means a large number of pictures.
explain: «Small details help police a lot.» Here a lot is an adverb meaning very much. Try the swap: «Small details help police very much» still makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: Sometimes a lot is a noun: a piece of land, such as a parking lot, or a thing sold at an auction. Read the whole sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits.
fact: A lot and lots mean a large number or a large amount.
fact: «A lot» can be an adverb meaning very much or very often, as in «help a lot».
fact: «Lots of room» means a large amount of space.
fact: A parking lot is a car park (USA, Canada).
fact: In maths, «a lot» is not an exact number; the problem gives the real numbers.
exercise: «Most grown-ups spend a third of their weekdays at work, and a lot of what you hear at home is that work leaking in.» In this sentence, a lot of means? | *A large amount of | A piece of land | Very often | A thing sold at an auction
exercise: «When passing a horse and rider you slow down, give lots of room and say hello.» What does lots of room mean? | A room for a horse | A place to sell things at an auction | A few small rooms | *A large amount of space
exercise: In the USA, what is a parking lot? | A large number of cars | A group of cars for sale | A kind of road | *A car park
test: «Animation is lots of still pictures, shown so fast that they blend into movement.» What does lots mean here? | A thing sold at an auction | *A large number | A piece of land | A kind of trick
test: What is a lot at an auction? | *A thing or group of things sold | A kind of prize | A measure of time | A place to park
exam: «Small details help police a lot.» What is a lot doing in this sentence? | *An adverb meaning very much | A parking space | A number of police | A noun meaning a piece of land
